= Lodging and Hotel Accommodations

== Corporate Lodging Philosophy

Noice & Toit LLP partners with leading international hotel groups (including Marriott, Hyatt, and Accor) to provide comfortable, safe, and productive lodging for our professionals worldwide. Business travel can be physically demanding; our accommodations standard ensures employees enjoy secure, quiet, and well-located lodging without incurring extravagant costs.

All hotel accommodations must be booked through our corporate travel portal, which grants access to negotiated corporate rates, complimentary high-speed internet, and flexible cancellation terms.

== Regional Nightly Room Rate Caps

Nightly room caps are established based on prevailing hotel market rates across our primary travel destinations. These caps apply to the base room rate per night, exclusive of mandatory municipal occupancy taxes and value-added tax (VAT).

=== Tier 1: Major Financial and Global Metropolises
- *Cap*: Up to *€220.00* / *\$250.00* / *£190.00* per night.
- *Applicable Locations*: London, New York City, San Francisco, Zurich, Geneva, Paris, Tokyo, Singapore, and Hong Kong.

=== Tier 2: Established Regional Business Hubs
- *Cap*: Up to *€160.00* / *\$180.00* / *£140.00* per night.
- *Applicable Locations*: Berlin, Munich, Frankfurt, Amsterdam, Dublin, Chicago, Boston, Seattle, Toronto, Sydney, and Milan.

=== Tier 3: Secondary Cities and Regional Markets
- *Cap*: Up to *€120.00* / *\$140.00* / *£105.00* per night.
- *Applicable Locations*: All other secondary metropolitan areas, university towns, suburban office parks, and provincial destinations.

#card-do("Stay within regional lodging caps")[
  Select standard single rooms within the designated nightly cap for your destination city. When traveling during major industry trade events (such as the Munich Oktoberfest, London International Law Week, or UN General Assembly) where rates spike across the entire city, obtain written manager email approval prior to booking above the cap.
]

#card-dont("Book executive suites or luxury boutique properties")[
  Never book multi-room executive suites, penthouse accommodations, luxury resort villas, or five-star flagship properties (e.g., Four Seasons, Ritz-Carlton) unless a client contract explicitly requires accommodation at a specific venue and reimburses the full cost without markup.
]

== Folio Substantiation and Incidental Auditing

When checking out of a hotel, always obtain an itemized checkout folio. Do not rely on initial booking confirmations, prepayment receipts, or mobile app summaries. The final checkout folio is essential because it details every individual charge posted to your room account during your stay.

#card-do("Scrutinize and itemize your checkout folio")[
  Carefully inspect your folio upon checkout. Confirm that the room rate matches your booking confirmation and verify that local taxes are itemized. Mark any personal non-reimbursable charges and deduct them before submitting your expense claim.
]

#card-dont("Claim hotel minibar, movie, or wellness charges")[
  Charges incurred for in-room minibar snacks and alcoholic beverages, pay-per-view movies, spa therapies, in-room gaming, and premium health club surcharges are strictly personal expenditures. Finance will deduct all minibar and entertainment lines from your reimbursement.
]

=== City Taxes, Resort Fees, and Mandatory Levies
Mandatory municipal hotel occupancy taxes, tourism promotion levies (such as the Paris Taxe de Séjour or Berlin City Tax), and mandatory facility fees are fully reimbursable when itemized on the official checkout folio. However, voluntary amenity bundles or optional resort passes must not be accepted.

== Laundry and Dry Cleaning on Extended Assignments

Maintaining clean business attire is necessary when traveling on extended assignments, but laundry services should be utilized sensibly.

#card-do("Expense laundry on trips exceeding five business days")[
  Employees traveling on continuous business trips extending beyond five (5) business days may claim reasonable laundry and garment pressing services up to a maximum limit of €35.00 / \$40.00 / £30.00 per seven-day period.
]

#card-dont("Charge rush laundry on short trips")[
  Do not charge hotel same-day rush dry cleaning or express pressing services on short trips of two to four days. Pack sufficient business attire to cover short journeys without resorting to premium hotel valet services.
]

== Extended Stay Apartments and Serviced Residences

When an assignment requires an employee to remain in a client city for more than fourteen (14) consecutive calendar days:
- Work with the Noice & Toit Travel Desk to evaluate serviced apartment providers (e.g., Citadines, Frasers, Sonder).
- Serviced apartments typically offer weekly housekeeping, equipped kitchenettes, and high-speed internet at rates 30% to 50% below standard hotel rooms.
- Grocery purchases for meal preparation in serviced apartments are reimbursable under the daily meal allowance provisions described in Chapter 7.

== Hotel Loyalty Perks and Room Upgrades

Employees may participate in hotel loyalty programs and collect loyalty points for personal use:
- Complimentary room upgrades awarded by hotels based on your elite loyalty tier are welcome, provided the firm is billed only for the baseline standard room rate.
- Employees must never pay an additional cash fee to upgrade their room category out of firm funds.
- Negotiated corporate rates usually include complimentary Wi-Fi and breakfast; check your corporate booking confirmation before purchasing hotel breakfast add-ons.

== Frequently Asked Questions

*Q: Are alternative lodging platforms like Airbnb or Vrbo permitted?*\
A: Yes, short-term rentals via approved platforms are permissible for multi-week stays or group project teams, provided the per-person nightly cost does not exceed the relevant regional city cap. The property must provide dedicated professional workspace, secure private access, and reliable high-speed internet.

*Q: What should I do if a hotel attempts to charge a no-show fee for a canceled trip?*\
A: If a trip is canceled due to client demands or illness, notify the hotel prior to the stated cancellation deadline. If a late cancellation fee is charged despite reasonable efforts, attach an explanation and client project code to the report; Finance will cover the charge upon Practice Leader sign-off.
